Z||000000||firstfiero||10-18-2001||02:51 PM||||     Just had to pass this story on guys. Today I pull into the parking lot of the bar my wife works at. As I'm getting out of my fiero The bar managers son,Who's sitting in a car next to me, asks what year it is. I tell him its and 86 and then he starts talking about his first car. He had an 86 1/2 gt. He starts talking about how he had everything down to the v6 he could exhaust, ram air, port and polished. Then when he starts talking about takeing out his sail panels because their cracked I suddenly remembered a fiero I looked at for my best friends wife about 4 months ago. It had the big tips on the back and was the same year. They only want 800 bucks for it at some little crap car dealer down town. My friend had sold me a his knotchback because he wanted a fastback and his wife was looking for one for him to hide till christmas. Anyway I ask him if the interiore had been made red and he says yes. Then I ask him where he got rid of it at and he says the same car dealer down town. Damn I knew that was good deal for 800 bucks! He swares he had about 3 grand into the engine. Anyway we talked about fiero's for about an hour. It was nice to talk to someone who loves the cars as much as I do. Sorry this so long winded but sometimes I'm stunned at how small a world it is. I hope she bought that car.... I think she's afraid that I'd tell him so she won't come clean with the info. lol<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000001||Dave Gunsul||10-19-2001||12:45 AM||||That would be nice to have happen just once.<BR>I went in to buy oil for an oil change today and was wearing my NIFE hat and jacket. The <BR>checkout lady looked at me and asked: "what's a Fiero?"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><BR>I told her that it was the only mid engine sports car made in America. As i'm walking out I was thinking that she probably didn't know what a mid-engined car was either.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>This lady wasn't young or anything either she was in her 30's, oh well.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||5
